# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build intermediates. Regenerated by ./build.sh; never belong in a diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built artifacts. This repo is source-only: zips and APKs are attached to
# GitHub releases, not committed, so history stays diffable.
# Rebuild any of them with the component's ./build.sh, which runs its tests
# first and refuses to package if they fail.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APK signing keystores. Each tile APK is signed with its own
# keystore/debug.jks, generated by build.sh if absent.
#
# These are development keys with a known password and protect nothing, but
# publishing one lets anyone sign an "update" to an already-installed app.
# They are kept locally -- do not delete them: Android refuses to upgrade an
# installed app whose signature changed, so losing a key forces an
# uninstall/reinstall and loses that app's data and permission grants.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/keystore/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reverse-engineering evidence and proprietary reference material.
#
# As of 2026-10-22 these no longer live here at all -- they were moved OUT of
# the repository working tree to ../thor/, because .gitignore alone is not
# protection: a routine `git clean -xfd` deletes ignored files, which would
# have destroyed the reference APKs and this unit's factory sensor-calibration
# backup. Git cannot touch anything above its root.
#
# These entries are kept as a guard, so that recreating either of them here
# cannot accidentally be committed. Do not move the real directories back in.
#
# `upstream/` is gone entirely: the one ticket draft it held now sits beside
# CLAUDE.md as `lineageos-display-rotation.local.md`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
findings/
reference/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working documents that drive development. Local only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
PRIORITIES.md
AYN-BUTTON-PANEL.md
NEXT-SESSION-PROMPT*.md
README-dev.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-component scratchpads. One per module/app, holding evidence pointers and
# working notes -- the "see the research notes" material that is deliberately
# absent from the published READMEs.
#
# Convention: <component>/NOTES.local.md. The `.local.md` suffix is what is
# ignored, so any local-only document can use it at any depth and cannot be
# committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.local.md
